[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2906853030","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106764#issuecomment-2906853030","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106764","id":2906853030,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tQw6m","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-24T14:13:41Z","updated_at":"2025-05-24T14:13:41Z","body":"This isn't a bug, this is how single line statements like this works, it's equivalent to:\n```gdscript\nif false:\n    print(\"before\")\n    @warning_ignore(\"incompatible_ternary\") print(\"after\")\n```\nNot:\n```gdscript\nif false:\n    print(\"before\")\n@warning_ignore(\"incompatible_ternary\") print(\"after\")\n```\n\nSee:\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/90016\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/77277\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/6924","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2906853030/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2907003977","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106764#issuecomment-2907003977","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106764","id":2907003977,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tRVxJ","user":{"login":"Kaleb-Reid","id":78945904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTQ1OTA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78945904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid","html_url":"https://github.com/Kaleb-Reid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-24T20:12:18Z","updated_at":"2025-05-24T20:47:44Z","body":"@AThousandShips you kind of just proved my point that this behaviour is at minimum not intuitive (I would still consider this a bug) because your first code snippet is not equivalent to mine. My example, having the ```@warning_ignore(...)```, behaves the same as your second code snippet.\n\nHere's another example:\n```\nif false: @warning_ignore(\"incompatible_ternary\") print(\"here\")\n```\nis currently equivalent to writing:\n```\nif false: pass\n@warning_ignore(\"incompatible_ternary\") print(\"here\")\n```\nOnce again ```@warning_ignore_start(...)``` and ```@warning_ignore_restore(...)``` don't have this problem because if you try to use them in this way they result in a syntax error of ```Expected newline after a standalone annotation.```, a rule which it seems like ```@warning_ignore(...)``` should also follow.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2907003977/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2907792953","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106764#issuecomment-2907792953","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106764","id":2907792953,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tUWY5","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-25T12:18:19Z","updated_at":"2025-05-25T12:18:19Z","body":"Warning annotations only consider lines, not columns. Using multiple statements on a single line is not a recommended style and and may not even work as expected, as AThousandShips mentioned above.\n\nI agree that this is a rather debatable issue, but it seems to me that the indentation syntax implies that the primary supported option is \"one statement per line\". Short notations have a secondary level of support, we cannot always fix or deprecate them without breaking compatibility.\n\nIn this case, however, it may indeed be considered a bug. We could fix it by considering not only lines but also columns. The question is whether we should go for this complication, given that this is a rather rare edge case.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2907792953/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2918805757","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106764#issuecomment-2918805757","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106764","id":2918805757,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6t-XD9","user":{"login":"Kaleb-Reid","id":78945904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTQ1OTA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78945904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid","html_url":"https://github.com/Kaleb-Reid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-29T09:15:22Z","updated_at":"2025-05-29T09:15:22Z","body":"@dalexeev Yes it may not be recommended to write GDScript in this way but I figured that the issue might as well be raised in case anyone wanted to increase consistency. I also only found this behaviour while testing a plugin which specifically inlines GDScript as a method of obfuscation.\nI looked for a bit but I couldn't figure out where the other ```@warning_ignore_...``` annotations print errors upon following them with something other than a newline. Do these annotations take columns into account for the errors?\nAlso, is adding the errors mostly a problem of breaking compatibility?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2918805757/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2919824005","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106764#issuecomment-2919824005","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106764","id":2919824005,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6uCPqF","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-29T15:48:00Z","updated_at":"2025-05-29T15:48:00Z","body":"> Also, is adding the errors mostly a problem of breaking compatibility?\n\nYes, it is a significant concern, we should not break compatibility without a good reason. It is much more important than the discussed problem, which is easy to work around and unlikely to occur. But I think we will fix it sooner or later. It just should not be unnecessarily complex and it is a low priority.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2919824005/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]